// @contract: C-015
// Graduated from proofs/wall-corpus/unique_non_flat_element.almd at the
// commissioning switchover: the structural emitter compares non-flat heap
// elements by deep CONTENT equality, so unique over List[List[String]]
// dedups correctly instead of refusing.
// list.unique over a NON-FLAT heap element (List[String] elements own
// further heap): the _hshare slot-wise eq is exact only for flat scalar
// blocks, and a String-bearing element would compare HANDLES — two equal
// values mis-compare as distinct (the old silent-wrong-dedup class). The
// router refuses via the unregistered _x name; this fixture pins it (#1481).
fn f(xs: List[List[String]]) -> List[List[String]] = list.unique(xs)

effect fn main() -> Unit = println(int.to_string(list.len(f([
  ["a"],
  ["b"]
]))))
